research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-36.notes.md:28:The required `qftx-susy-algebra-and-multiplets` page contains `pthm-qftx-n2-bps-saturation-kernel-equivalence` and `def-qftx-bps-state-and-saturation`. Both direct supplier Step 1 records remain `escalated`. The theorem's actual conditional result and complete proof were inspected: it is restricted to a massive rest fiber with metric `(-,+,+,+)`, `epsilon_12=1`, natural units `hbar=c=1`, scalar central charge, actual Hilbert adjoints and a common product domain, and `AC_omega`; it proves an algebraic saturation/kernel equivalence, not existence or topologicality of a physical defect. At the initial supplier check, the theorem record cited four missing `aqft-susy-math-foundations` records (`lem-qftx-n1-chiral-superspace-identities`, `lem-qftx-supercharge-positive-energy-pairing`, `def-qftx-graded-trace-class-index-data`, `thm-qftx-witten-index-beta-independence`) and missing records for all four `qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model` items. A later fresh `loadStep1Record`/`step1Decision` check finds all eight lower-level items now `ready`: the four above and `lem-qftx-su2-compact-nonabelian-invariant-form`, `post-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-model`, `pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-classical-gauge-invariance`, and `pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-euler-lagrange`. The two direct `qftx-susy-algebra-and-multiplets` items themselves remain `escalated` with those old reasons, leaving a stale supplier readiness record for owner review. The page edge remains `open`; this batch makes no supersymmetry, BPS, or defect-realization claim. Draft status and precheck status alone were not treated as gaps.
