research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-56.notes.md:68:Theorem carrier audit: an existing assigned-path theorem draft was found and checked against the current item contract. I repaired the proof rather than assuming its original steps were complete. The local derivative isomorphism is now shown on the whole slice product by gauge-action conjugacy, after a uniform small-slice Neumann bound; properness excludes far returns. The Lie-algebra kernel argument now exponentiates a holonomy-centralizing value and uses the finite stabilizer to conclude it vanishes. The smooth-space proof spells out the local lift through the finite central quotient, regularity bootstrap for the Coulomb equation, convergence in every Sobolev order, and openness for the actual smooth quotient topology. Added explicit Sobolev algebra/embedding direct inputs for this bootstrap. Direct in-run suppliers are the configuration definition (level 2), gauge calculus (3), stabilizer/properness (4), and rough Green splitting (5), so this theorem is level 6. External premises are the Banach implicit/inverse theorems, Neumann perturbation, elliptic regularity, full AC, and higher-order Sobolev multiplication/embedding. Sources remain Walpuski §§5.13.2–5.13.3 and Williams §4.4, with their scope limits described above. No missing prerequisite identified; final proof-layout/source/contract checks remain pending.
