research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-frontier-append-1/preimages/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-4-notes.md:29:- `lem-qftx-bv-canonical-action-generates-brst-differential` (level 3; dependency: BV definition): explicitly computes the right-derivative sign for each field/ghost parity, proving `(S,Φ)=s₀Φ`; the local-field identity is conditional on well-defined variational derivatives and boundary behavior. Sources: GPS §§4.2, 4.6; QZ §§3.1–3.2, 4.2.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-frontier-append-1/preimages/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-4-notes.md:30:- `lem-qftx-bv-master-equation-brst-nilpotence` (level 3; dependency: BV definition): proves both directions between the CME and nilpotence of `sF=(S_BV,F)` from shifted Jacobi. The converse explicitly assumes no nonzero ghost-number-one central element; it is verified for the finite canonical polynomial algebra and remains a separate hypothesis for any formal local-functional domain. Sources: GPS §§4.2–4.3, 4.6; QZ §§4.2–4.4.
