research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/gauge-slice-prerequisite-scaffold.md:25:Start with integer k > dim(M)/2 + 1, H^k connections, H^(k+1) gauge transformations, a smooth reference connection and a finite bundle atlas. Define smooth section topology and quotient topology explicitly. Prove properness as well as the near-identity IFT chart: the latter alone cannot exclude a far gauge transformation returning to a small slice. Imported elliptic Green theory has smooth coefficients; author its needed rough-coefficient extension. Prove regularity compatibility to obtain the C-infinity bundle. Mitter–Viallet Theorems5.28–5.29 and Narasimhan–Ramadas §§2–4 guide the reconstruction but do not waive their referenced auxiliary steps.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/gauge-slice-source-repair.md:13:3. The native Mitter–Viallet and Singer source-fetch stamps remain unresolved; the current check still reports only one of three sources verified. A successful web PDF read is not a successful Node fetch, and no fetch stamp has been created.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/gauge-slice-source-repair.md:22:[Mitter–Viallet, CMP 79 (1981), 457–472](https://scispace.com/pdf/on-the-bundle-of-connections-and-the-gauge-orbit-manifold-in-1nks9qpdkj.pdf): this repair read targeted §§II–V, especially printed pp. 464–472. The earlier author's full-paper reading remains their own evidence; it is not reassigned to this reviewer. The actual main principal-bundle theorem is **5.28**, with Hilbert-manifold Theorem **5.29**, preceded by the detailed local derivative calculation in Proposition **5.6**. Proposition **4.4**'s global effectiveness of the slice refers to earlier proofs, while rough-coefficient elliptic surjectivity refers to Narasimhan–Ramadas Proposition 3.3. A citation to its inverse-function calculation alone cannot discharge properness or the non-near-identity uniqueness issue.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/gauge-slice-source-repair.md:24:[Narasimhan–Ramadas, CMP 67 (1979), 121–136](https://scispace.com/pdf/geometry-of-su-2-gauge-fields-3mpojvnw66.pdf): newly recovered primary fulltext; read targeted §§1–6, pp. 121–132. Its §§2–3 give detailed properness, multiplier and rough-coefficient elliptic arguments; §4 obtains principal bundles from a proper free split action. The latter general-action result must itself be reconstructed via the local inverse function theorem and properness. §§5–6 give an independent obstruction through left-invariant connections and a nontrivial finite-dimensional SO(3) matrix bundle. This is a valuable proof cross-check for the trivial SU(2)/S3 problem; it does not replace the arbitrary SU(N)/S4 sectors. Section 7 was not read.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-owner-resolution/gauge-slice-source-repair.md:26:All seven prior Singer failed access records and the five prior native Mitter failures were reused, not erased. Newly investigated routes include legacy Euclid download and article URLs (200 responses containing only approximately 1.1 KB HTML), Springer PDF (approximately 3 KB HTML cookie page), INSPIRE API (metadata without a document payload), and the new SciSpace Singer fulltext (actual six-page PDF extraction through web; shell HTTP 403/919-byte HTML). The author-hosted Mitter path found by a different search is `https://www.lpthe.jussieu.fr/~viallet/mitter_viallet_cmp_1981.pdf`: indexed full text was visible once, but fresh HTTPS/HTTP requests both returned 404, and the bare host failed DNS. It is not an honest replacement fetch stamp. A Hatcher fulltext request timed out; no new Hatcher or Toda reading is claimed. [source-reading.json](gauge-slice-source-repair/source-reading.json) records these boundaries.
