### Batch-56 example carriers

`ex-qftx-covariantly-constant-stabilizer` now distinguishes the based stabilizer (trivial for every connection by parallel transport) from the full irreducible stabilizer (`Z_N`) and the reduced stabilizer (trivial). Its direct mathematical suppliers are the configuration definition and stabilizer/holonomy lemma; the maximum in-run level is 4, so it is level 5. Walpuski supports the general holonomy-centralizer interface; Williams is recorded only as an abelian based/unbased comparison.

`ex-qftx-coulomb-chart-linearization` states the typed derivative of the Coulomb action map and verifies both inverse composites, including the one-derivative loss and all Sobolev orders. Its direct suppliers are the configuration definition, gauge calculus, rough Green splitting, and the principal-bundle theorem; theorem level 6 makes this consumer level 7. Walpuski supports the general Coulomb chart; Williams is an abelian comparison, while the SU(N) inverse is computed locally. Neither example assumes a physics model or uses empirical claims. Their proof contracts, source coverage, page placement, and readiness checks remain to be assembled after final carrier review.

