# Gauge-slice source and prerequisite resolution

Run: `advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23`. Reviewer: `/root/gauge_slice_source_repair`. Date: 2026-10-23. This is owner evidence and a concrete prerequisite proposal, not native acceptance, readiness, or a completed Singer proof. No controller, gate, readiness, imported mathematics, main plan, or another author's active scope was changed.

The missing approved item remains `thm-qftx-singer-global-gauge-section-obstruction` on `qftx-gauge-slice-mathematics`. It must not be dropped or replaced with the finite-dimensional Jacobian theorem. Singer's full primary paper has now actually been read through a distinct fulltext mirror, resolving the absence of its exact statement. The obstruction still needs substantial locally authored mathematics. The existing four-carrier batch does not supply that mathematics.

The concrete proposal is [gauge-slice-prerequisite-plan.json](gauge-slice-prerequisite-plan.json): three new A/B pairs, eighteen item contracts including four B examples, a local item DAG, exact proposed claims and proof obligations, source reading limits, consumer mappings, and twenty-six current published imported supplier candidates pinned to exact bytes and their current imported page homes. These are proposed interfaces for authoring, not claims that the proofs are already available locally. The three pairs separate analytic quotient construction, irreducible-family avoidance, and homotopy of gauge groups. Each belongs to `quantum-field-theory-mathematics`. Root must choose actual orders before the existing gauge-slice pair and preserve the existing fifty-five pair identities when integrating after writers drain.

