All original batch-3 manifests, notes, coverage, cross-batch evidence, contracts, and both native result carriers were copied without overwriting existing archives. The two edited B-example source preimages were separately retained before edits. See [preimages.json](gauge-slice-source-repair/preimages.json). Original native results and readiness rows were not edited. The root-owned rehash/recertification remains necessary for the changed source/contract bytes.

## Actual authoritative reading

[Singer, CMP 60 (1978), 7–12](https://scispace.com/pdf/some-remarks-on-the-gribov-ambiguity-33y52evtqe.pdf): read the complete extracted six-page paper, including §§1–2, Theorems 1–9, Corollary 4, and references; printed pp. 9–10 were also requested through the PDF screenshot route. This is the primary paper mirrored by SciSpace, not its catalogue abstract. No local raw PDF byte archive or native fetch stamp is claimed. It supplies the exact C-infinity configuration/gauge topology, irreducible restriction, finite-center quotient, and sphere hypotheses. Theorem 1 refers to Ebin/Palais analysis. Theorem 2 sketches avoidance of the infinite-codimension reducible locus; it does not prove the required local avoidance machinery in detail. Theorem 5 sketches the hemisphere argument and refers to parametric smoothing. The low SU(N) homotopy values are imported from Toda. Reading that paper is therefore not a complete reconstruction of its dependencies.

[Mitter–Viallet, CMP 79 (1981), 457–472](https://scispace.com/pdf/on-the-bundle-of-connections-and-the-gauge-orbit-manifold-in-1nks9qpdkj.pdf): this repair read targeted §§II–V, especially printed pp. 464–472. The earlier author's full-paper reading remains their own evidence; it is not reassigned to this reviewer. The actual main principal-bundle theorem is **5.28**, with Hilbert-manifold Theorem **5.29**, preceded by the detailed local derivative calculation in Proposition **5.6**. Proposition **4.4**'s global effectiveness of the slice refers to earlier proofs, while rough-coefficient elliptic surjectivity refers to Narasimhan–Ramadas Proposition 3.3. A citation to its inverse-function calculation alone cannot discharge properness or the non-near-identity uniqueness issue.

[Narasimhan–Ramadas, CMP 67 (1979), 121–136](https://scispace.com/pdf/geometry-of-su-2-gauge-fields-3mpojvnw66.pdf): newly recovered primary fulltext; read targeted §§1–6, pp. 121–132. Its §§2–3 give detailed properness, multiplier and rough-coefficient elliptic arguments; §4 obtains principal bundles from a proper free split action. The latter general-action result must itself be reconstructed via the local inverse function theorem and properness. §§5–6 give an independent obstruction through left-invariant connections and a nontrivial finite-dimensional SO(3) matrix bundle. This is a valuable proof cross-check for the trivial SU(2)/S3 problem; it does not replace the arbitrary SU(N)/S4 sectors. Section 7 was not read.

